\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Continuous-frame Fourier spectrum, Tikhonov regularization, and sharp Paley--Wiener bounds. (a) Continuous-frame Fourier multiplier $\mathaccent "0365{G}_w(k_\perp )$ and Tikhonov signal transfer $T_{\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ ($\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}} = 10^{-2}, 10^{-3}$) with Paley--Wiener passband $\mathcal  {H}_{k_{\max }}$ shaded up to $w k_{\max } = 1.394$; inset shows the deconvolution noise gain $\mathaccent "0365{H}_{w,\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ peaking at $(2\sqrt  {\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}})^{-1}$ [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:noise_multiplier}]. (b) Sharp Paley--Wiener bounds $A(w,k_{\max }), B = 1$ and condition number $\kappa (S_{w,k_{\max }}) = B/A$ versus $w k_{\max }$ [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:pw_bounds}], highlighting both the weak-attenuation regime ($w k_{\max } = 0.604 \to A = 0.833, \kappa = 1.20$) and the moderate-aperture benchmark ($w k_{\max } = 1.394 \to A = 0.378, \kappa = 2.64$, corresponding to $\mathrm  {NA} = 0.20$ at $w/\lambda = 1.11$).}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frame_regularization}{{2}{5}{Continuous-frame Fourier spectrum, Tikhonov regularization, and sharp Paley--Wiener bounds. (a) Continuous-frame Fourier multiplier $\widetilde {G}_w(k_\perp )$ and Tikhonov signal transfer $T_{\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ ($\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}} = 10^{-2}, 10^{-3}$) with Paley--Wiener passband $\mathcal {H}_{k_{\max }}$ shaded up to $w k_{\max } = 1.394$; inset shows the deconvolution noise gain $\widetilde {H}_{w,\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ peaking at $(2\sqrt {\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}})^{-1}$ [Eq.~\eqref {eq:noise_multiplier}]. (b) Sharp Paley--Wiener bounds $A(w,k_{\max }), B = 1$ and condition number $\kappa (S_{w,k_{\max }}) = B/A$ versus $w k_{\max }$ [Eq.~\eqref {eq:pw_bounds}], highlighting both the weak-attenuation regime ($w k_{\max } = 0.604 \to A = 0.833, \kappa = 1.20$) and the moderate-aperture benchmark ($w k_{\max } = 1.394 \to A = 0.378, \kappa = 2.64$, corresponding to $\mathrm {NA} = 0.20$ at $w/\lambda = 1.11$)}{figure.2}{}}
